From 5f946f75872d1916f5decbd15f8df089b45c2ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Musichen <alex.musichen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:36:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs(platform): the platform is Acryl plus Cordis plugins;
 DeepSeek Harness is one agent driver

/docs/platform still framed ACRYL as "a clean plugin layer over DeepSeek Harness": its install section was `dsh plugin --profile desktop add <package>`, and the compatibility contract's five items were about DSH bundles, the Harness client surface and DSH service names.

- The lede, the install section and the contract now describe what 1.0 ships: a Cordis plugin platform whose web framework is Acryl (router, Node server, db and kv ports, live state, JSX), apps as folders of plugins mounted from blend.yaml, dependencies as service names, a versioned public surface with acrylblends upgrade, and ACRYL capabilities as additive and optional.
- A 1.0 notice says the thing the page used to imply otherwise: DeepSeek Harness is not the platform. It is one agent driver - the ACP driver runs any agent that speaks the Agent Client Protocol, and dsh is its first preset - and an app that starts no agent depends on neither.
- The runtime-layers stack gains the missing middle: ACRYL (the product), Acryl (the framework), Cordis (the runtime).
- The footer note on every page said "Built on Cordis and DeepSeek Harness"; it now says an agent joins as a driver, so the app is not tied to one.
